---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AdSlot from '../components/AdSlot.astro';
import AffiliateCard from '../components/AffiliateCard.astro';
import digitalProducts from '../data/digital-products.json';

const bookProduct = digitalProducts.find(p => p.id === 'power-without-the-panic-book');
const toolkitProduct = digitalProducts.find(p => p.id === 'nigerian-solar-toolkit-bundle');

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "Band A Electricity Tariff vs Petrol Generator vs Solar: 2026 Nigeria Payback & Cost Index",
  "description": "Comprehensive economic research analyzing monthly power expenses under Band A DISCO tariffs (₦209/kWh) and petrol (₦1,150/L) against LiFePO4 solar payback periods in Nigeria.",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Reid Caster Publishing"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "IbadanSolarHub",
    "url": "https://ibadansolarhub.com.ng"
  },
  "datePublished": "2026-09-16",
  "mainEntityOfPage": "https://ibadansolarhub.com.ng/band-a-tariff-vs-solar-index"
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Band A Electricity Tariff vs Petrol Generator vs Solar: 2026 Nigeria Payback Index"
  description="Comprehensive 2026 Nigerian power cost index. Compare Band A DISCO tariffs (₦209/kWh) and petrol generator fuel against turnkey LiFePO4 solar installation payback periods."
  schema={schema}
>
  {/* Hero Header */}
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-slate-900 via-slate-800 to-slate-900 text-white py-14 md:py-20 border-b border-slate-800 relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(#f59e0b_1px,transparent_1px)] [background-size:24px_24px] opacity-10"></div>
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10 text-center">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 bg-solar-500/10 text-solar-400 border border-solar-500/20 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold mb-4">
        📊 2026 Nigerian Energy Economics Whitepaper
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black tracking-tight leading-tight max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        Band A Electricity Tariff vs. Petrol Generator vs. Solar: <span class="text-solar-400">The 2026 Payback Index</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-300 max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        With Band A DISCO tariffs elevated at <strong>₦209 – ₦225 per kWh</strong> and petrol fluctuating at <strong>₦1,050 – ₦1,250 per litre</strong>, what is the fastest way to stop burning cash on power? Here is the exact mathematical payback model.
      </p>
      
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400">
        <span>Author: <strong class="text-white">Reid Caster Publishing</strong></span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>Data Updated: <strong class="text-white">September 2026</strong></span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>Reading Time: <strong class="text-white">7 Mins</strong></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 md:py-14">
    
    {/* Executive Summary Card */}
    <div class="bg-amber-500/10 border-2 border-solar-500/30 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950 flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        ⚡ Executive Key Finding
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-800 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed">
        A standard middle-class Nigerian household (3-bedroom flat or duplex) combining Band A grid electricity with 5–6 hours of generator backup spends an average of <strong>₦240,000 to ₦490,000 monthly</strong> on power. At current equipment prices, an engineered <strong>3.5kVA – 5kVA Lithium (LiFePO4) solar system</strong> fully amortizes itself in <strong>8.5 to 13.5 months</strong>. Over a 10-year battery lifespan, solar saves between <strong>₦18,000,000 and ₦42,000,000</strong> compared to grid-plus-generator operation.
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* Section 1: The Three Power Profiles */}
    <div class="prose max-w-none mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">
        1. Side-by-Side Financial Comparison Table
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Below is an empirical cost analysis across three real Nigerian household profiles using verified 2026 market figures:
      </p>

      {/* Comparison Grid Table */}
      <div class="overflow-x-auto shadow-sm rounded-xl border border-slate-200 mb-8">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm border-collapse bg-white">
          <thead class="bg-slate-900 text-white font-bold">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">Household Profile</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">Monthly Band A Bill</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">Monthly Fuel Bill (Gen)</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">Total Monthly Power Spend</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">Turnkey Solar Setup</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800 bg-solar-600 text-slate-950">Payback Breakeven</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">5-Yr Net Savings</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 text-slate-700">
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50 transition">
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">
                <strong>Starter / Remote Worker</strong><br>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-normal">1-2 Rooms, Laptops, Starlink, Fans, TV</span>
              </td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦30,000</td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦75,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(3 hrs/day Small Gen)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-red-600">₦105,000/mo</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">₦950,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(1.2kVA + 1.28kWh LiFePO4)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-extrabold text-green-700 bg-emerald-50">9.0 Months</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-slate-900">₦5,350,000</td>
            </tr>

            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50 transition bg-amber-50/30">
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">
                <strong>Essential Home</strong><br>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-normal">2-3 Bed Flat, Inverter Fridge, TV, Fans</span>
              </td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦70,000</td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦145,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(5 hrs/day 3.5kVA Gen)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-red-600">₦215,000/mo</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">₦2,150,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(2.5kVA + 2.56kWh LiFePO4)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-extrabold text-green-700 bg-emerald-50">10.0 Months</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-slate-900">₦10,750,000</td>
            </tr>

            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50 transition">
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">
                <strong>Standard Comfort (Deep Freezer)</strong><br>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-normal">3-Bed Duplex, Freezer, Fridge, Water Dispenser</span>
              </td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦95,000</td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦180,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(6 hrs/day Gen)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-red-600">₦275,000/mo</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">₦3,100,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(3.5kVA + 5.12kWh LiFePO4)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-extrabold text-green-700 bg-emerald-50">11.2 Months</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-slate-900">₦13,400,000</td>
            </tr>

            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50 transition bg-solar-50/40">
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">
                <strong>Whole-Home + Inverter AC</strong><br>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-normal">4-Bed Duplex, 1.5HP AC, Pump, Deep Freezer</span>
              </td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦160,000</td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦290,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(8 hrs/day 7.5kVA Gen)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-red-600">₦450,000/mo</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">₦4,600,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(5kVA + 10.24kWh LiFePO4)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-extrabold text-green-700 bg-emerald-50">10.2 Months</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-slate-900">₦22,400,000</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 2: Why Band A is not 24/7 Independence */}
    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm mb-12 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">
        2. The "Band A Illusion" vs. Real Grid Performance in Nigeria
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed">
        Many consumers initially believed paying <strong>₦209/kWh</strong> under Band A would solve power reliability. However, empirical field data from IBEDC, EKEDC, IKEDC, and AEDC shows three structural points of failure:
      </p>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-2">
        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <div class="text-amber-600 font-bold text-sm mb-1">⚡ Grid Collapse Exposure</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            When the National Grid collapses (multiple incidents recorded each quarter), Band A feeders drop immediately to zero volts regardless of billing tariff.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <div class="text-amber-600 font-bold text-sm mb-1">🌧️ Distribution Transformer Faults</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Localized feeder cable cutoffs, fallen poles during rainy seasons, and blown substation fuses leave Band A neighborhoods in the dark for days.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <div class="text-amber-600 font-bold text-sm mb-1">💸 Compound Tariff Increases</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Unlike Solar (where your Levelized Cost of Electricity is locked for 10–25 years), Band A tariffs adjust continuously upward to match exchange rates.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 3: The 3 Cost Mistakes Nigerian Buyers Make */}
    <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 mb-12 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-solar-400">
        3. The Three Cost Calculation Mistakes To Avoid
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-300">
        <div class="border-l-4 border-solar-500 pl-4 py-1">
          <strong class="text-white">Mistake #1: Omitting Generator Hidden Costs</strong>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">
            A generator doesn't just consume fuel. Engine oil changes (₦4,500 every 100 hours), spark plugs, carburetor servicing, noise pollution stress, and emergency midnight repairs add ₦25,000 – ₦50,000 monthly to your real cost.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border-l-4 border-solar-500 pl-4 py-1">
          <strong class="text-white">Mistake #2: Confusing Tubular vs. Lithium Battery Payback</strong>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">
            Tubular batteries seem cheaper initially, but only provide 50% Depth of Discharge and die within 2 to 3 years in Nigeria's tropical heat. Quality LiFePO4 Lithium batteries last 10+ years (4,000+ cycles) and allow 80%–90% discharge, making them 50% cheaper over 5 years.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border-l-4 border-solar-500 pl-4 py-1">
          <strong class="text-white">Mistake #3: Undersizing Solar Panels</strong>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">
            Installing a 5kVA inverter with only 2 or 4 solar panels forces the system to rely on grid/generator charging. To achieve genuine zero-fuel operation, your panel array must generate at least 1.25x your daily kilowatt-hour demand.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 4: Interactive Calculator CTA */}
    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-solar-500 to-amber-400 rounded-2xl p-8 text-slate-950 mb-12 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-black">Want to Calculate Your Exact Payback?</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-900 text-sm mt-1 max-w-xl">
          Use our free 2026 Nigerian Solar Sizing Engine to audit your appliances, get exact kVA & Lithium battery specs, and generate a 1-click printable BOQ.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a 
        href="/calculator"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-slate-950 hover:bg-slate-900 text-white font-bold px-6 py-3.5 rounded-xl shadow-lg transition transform active:scale-95 text-sm whitespace-nowrap"
      >
        <span>Launch Solar Calculator</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M14 5l7 7m0 0l-7 7m7-7H3" />
        </svg>
      </a>
    </div>

    {/* Section 5: Authoritative Digital Guides (Monetization) */}
    <div class="mb-14">
      <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">
          Official Nigerian Solar Publications
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">
          Published by <strong>Reid Caster Publishing</strong> to protect Nigerian buyers from overpaying or buying substandard solar equipment.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        {bookProduct && (
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-6 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between">
            <div>
              <div class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-amber-100 text-amber-900 rounded-md text-xs font-bold mb-3">
                Flagship Ebook (30 Chapters)
              </div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">{bookProduct.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1">Author: {bookProduct.author}</p>
              <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">
                {bookProduct.description}
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-slate-100 flex items-center justify-between">
              <div>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-400 block">Instant Download</span>
                <span class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900">₦{bookProduct.priceNgn.toLocaleString()}</span>
              </div>
              <a
                href={bookProduct.checkoutUrl}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-solar-500 hover:bg-solar-600 text-slate-950 font-bold px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl text-xs shadow transition"
              >
                Buy on Selar (₦{bookProduct.priceNgn.toLocaleString()})
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        )}

        {toolkitProduct && (
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-6 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between">
            <div>
              <div class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-blue-100 text-blue-900 rounded-md text-xs font-bold mb-3">
                Complete Tool Bundle (4-in-1)
              </div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">{toolkitProduct.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1">Publisher: {toolkitProduct.author}</p>
              <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">
                {toolkitProduct.description}
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-slate-100 flex items-center justify-between">
              <div>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-400 block">Instant Excel & PDF Bundle</span>
                <span class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900">₦{toolkitProduct.priceNgn.toLocaleString()}</span>
              </div>
              <a
                href={toolkitProduct.checkoutUrl}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-800 text-white font-bold px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl text-xs shadow transition"
              >
                Get Toolkit (₦{toolkitProduct.priceNgn.toLocaleString()})
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 6: Copyable Social Media Posts for Facebook & WhatsApp */}
    <div class="bg-slate-100 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 border border-slate-200">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 flex items-center gap-2">
          📱 Viral Social Posts (Ready to Share on Facebook & WhatsApp)
        </h3>
        <span class="text-xs bg-slate-200 text-slate-700 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full font-semibold">Copy & Share</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mb-4">
        Copy these pre-formatted posts directly into your Facebook Page, WhatsApp Status, or community groups to drive organic traffic back to IbadanSolarHub:
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        {/* Social Card 1 */}
        <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-300 text-xs text-slate-800 font-mono leading-relaxed relative">
          <p>
            🚨 <strong>THE NIGERIAN POWER REALITY CHECK: Band A vs Fuel vs Solar</strong><br><br>
            If you live in a 3-bedroom flat on Band A (paying ~₦70k/mo) and run a 3.5kVA generator for 5 hrs/day (spending ~₦145k/mo on petrol at ₦1,150/L):<br><br>
            ➡️ You are burning <strong>₦215,000 every month</strong> (₦2.58 Million every year) just on basic power.<br><br>
            💡 An engineered 2.5kVA - 3.5kVA Solar System with LiFePO4 Lithium costs ~₦2.15M – ₦3.1M turnkey. That means the solar system <strong>PAYS FOR ITSELF in under 11 months</strong>.<br><br>
            Every month after month 11 is 100% pure cash savings for the next 10 years.<br><br>
            👉 Audit your appliances & calculate your exact setup: https://ibadansolarhub.com.ng/band-a-tariff-vs-solar-index<br>
            📘 Official Guide by Reid Caster Publishing: https://selar.com/34ew22cs83
          </p>
        </div>

        {/* Social Card 2 */}
        <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-300 text-xs text-slate-800 font-mono leading-relaxed relative">
          <p>
            ⚠️ <strong>Before you pay a solar installer in Nigeria, ask these 3 questions:</strong><br><br>
            1. Are you quoting 50% Depth-of-Discharge Tubular batteries that die in 24 months, or 80% DoD LiFePO4 Lithium that lasts 10+ years?<br>
            2. Is there a DC Surge Protective Device (SPD) and DC breaker between my solar panels and inverter?<br>
            3. Did you size the panels for Nigerian peak sunshine (4.8 sun hours) so the battery actually hits 100% charge before 3 PM?<br><br>
            Don't waste millions on bad sizing. Download the complete Nigerian Solar Vetting Checklist & Load Calculator here:<br>
            👉 https://ibadansolarhub.com.ng/calculator
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
